0..70 Comment "// Values Rust holds cross into gandr as words, read by their layouts."
71..73 Comment "//"
74..147 Comment "// A Rust caller lends its memory and passes a word: a list\'s root, or an"
148..222 Comment "// `Option<&u32>`. Gandr reads the memory behind a word only by performing"
223..296 Comment "// `Memory.word` or `Memory.half`, which the caller\'s host answers at the"
297..373 Comment "// addresses it lent. The block\'s check admits both reads against their rows"
374..452 Comment "// under Rust\'s default layout. No reference crosses: gandr holds each word as"
453..465 Comment "// a number."
466..468 Comment "//"
469..544 Comment "// Each decoder reads a layout\'s memory type into the layout\'s data type. A"
545..623 Comment "// tagged word with its low bit set is the empty list, and any other addresses"
624..699 Comment "// a head and a tail. A packed word\'s low two bits tell the empty list, one"
700..775 Comment "// element inline, and a pointer to two elements and the rest. One `length`"
776..851 Comment "// over the list runs on each layout, transported along that layout\'s path."
852..925 Comment "// `derefOr` reads the null niche: the zero word is `None`, and any other"
926..1003 Comment "// addresses a `u32`. The Rust test calls these definitions and compares each"
1004..1027 Comment "// answer with its own."
1028..1030 Comment "//"
1031..1106 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-dispatcher/tests/boundary.rs` — the Rust caller"
1107..1183 Comment "// - see: `model/layouts/ribbit-list.gandr` — the two layouts and `length`"
1184..1265 Comment "// - see: `model/specification/niche-realizability.gandr` — `deref_or`\'s triple"
1267..1341 Comment "// The boundary check reads `admitBlock` here, whatever the listing names."
